1. What is DNA?
DNA (Deoxyribonucleic acid), the chemical basis of life that complexes with proteins to form the chromosomes. Structurally, DNA is a double helix-two thread like long strand of genetic material spiraled around each other. DNA is a polymer of deoxyribonucleotides composed of Base [Adenine (A), Thymine (T), Guanine (G), Cytosine (C)], Sugar and a Phosphate. The sequential arrangement of the individual nucleotides is responsible for giving uniqueness t…";}s:8:"relation";a:1:{s:10:"firstimage";s:0:"";}s:5:"title";N;s:11:"last_change";a:4:{s:4:"date";N;s:4:"user";N;s:2:"ip";N;s:3:"sum";N;}}s:10:"persistent";a:3:{s:4:"date";a:1:{s:7:"created";i:1773547242;}s:4:"user";s:0:"";s:7:"creator";s:0:"";}}